.env
.superpowers/
exports/

# dependencies (never track — includes symlinked node_modules in worktrees)
node_modules

# Engine's lock-bound dependency receipt lives beside node_modules. It must stay ignored so the
# generic clean-checkout update guard does not reject every correctly installed Splash checkout.
.splash-bun-install.json

# git worktrees created by the harness (EnterWorktree)
.claude/worktrees/
.splash-preflight.json

# per-install decor (lib/newsroom/state.ts) — written at the install root, never shared.
# Committing one would make every install of the release believe it is already migrated.
newsroom.json
.splash-runtime
.splash-instance-id
.sdd/

# packed delivery (scripts/pack-skills.mjs) — always derived from the repo, never committed.
.dist/

# The INSTALL's own newsroom profile, and its machine-readable cache. `NEWSROOM-PROFILE.example.md`
# is the tracked template; the real file belongs to whoever installed Splash and must never ship.
# Both were committed by accident on 2026-08-04 (swept into a docs commit by `git add -A`) carrying
# a real newsroom's colour, name and URL — so every stranger cloning this repository received that
# newsroom as their default, and every visual they made would have cited it as the source until
# they noticed. Found by the release dress rehearsal (registry A5), which is what that rehearsal is
# for: the defect is invisible from inside a working install, where the file is supposed to exist.
NEWSROOM-PROFILE.md
brand.json
